{
  "_doc": "Claude plan state (#344). Each case gives a reading (a claude_plan_usage_readings row, or null) and 'now'; expect is what claude_plan_usage.derive_state and summarize return. fresh_window_kinds lists the windows whose resets_at is after now, in reading order. Rules: a reading older than 24 h (strictly) is stale; a window is fresh only while resets_at > now; with no fresh weekly_all window the state is unknown; otherwise the worst fresh window decides: >= 100 exhausted, > 80 constrained, else available. Reset times in summary_line are shown in America/New_York as '%a %-I:%M %p'. Percentages are printed with no decimals: the exact binary value rounded half to even (Python f'{x:.0f}', Rust '{:.0}', Kotlin BigDecimal HALF_EVEN), so 23.5 -> 24, 80.5 -> 80, 62.5 -> 62. Java's %.0f and floor(x + 0.5) round half up and differ on those. The state always compares the unrounded value. Timestamps may carry any UTC offset (manual readings use -05:00, status line readings +00:00) and fractional seconds; compare them as instants, never as text. Optional per-case keys: note (a comment) and same_instant_as (another case with the same instants written in a different offset, which must expect the same result).",
  "version": 1,
